k_it_out-960x954.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/belgium_we_can_work_it_out-768x763.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/belgium_we_can_work_it_out-66x66.jpg 66w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/belgium_we_can_work_it_out.jpg 1000w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"9144\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/belgium_we_can_work_it_out/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/belgium_we_can_work_it_out.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1000,994\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"We Can Work It Out/Day Tripper single artwork – Belgium\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/belgium_we_can_work_it_out-960x954.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/denmark_we_can_work_it_out/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTk1IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDE5NSI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"195\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/denmark_we_can_work_it_out-200x195.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"We Can Work It Out single artwork - Denmark, Norway\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/denmark_we_can_work_it_out-200x195.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/denmark_we_can_work_it_out-580x565.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/denmark_we_can_work_it_out-960x935.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/denmark_we_can_work_it_out-768x748.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/denmark_we_can_work_it_out.jpg 1000w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"9279\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/denmark_we_can_work_it_out/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/denmark_we_can_work_it_out.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1000,974\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"We Can Work It Out single artwork – Denmark, Norway\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/denmark_we_can_work_it_out-960x935.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/japan_we_can_work_it_out/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_we_can_work_it_out-200x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"We Can Work It Out single artwork - Japan\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_we_can_work_it_out-200x200.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_we_can_work_it_out-580x578.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_we_can_work_it_out-960x956.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_we_can_work_it_out-768x765.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_we_can_work_it_out-66x66.jpg 66w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_we_can_work_it_out.jpg 1000w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"9605\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/japan_we_can_work_it_out/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_we_can_work_it_out.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1000,996\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"We Can Work It Out single artwork – Japan\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_we_can_work_it_out-960x956.jpg\"></a></div></figure></div><p>Two recording sessions were scheduled on this day. The first lasted from 2.30-6.30pm, and saw the rehearsal of ‘We Can Work It Out’ plus the taping of two takes of the rhythm track. This included bass guitar by <a href=\"/people/paul-mccartney/\">Paul McCartney</a>, drums by <a href=\"/people/ringo-starr/\">Ringo Starr</a>, <a href=\"/people/john-lennon/\">John Lennon</a>’s Gibson Jumbo acoustic guitar, and tambourine by <a href=\"/people/george-harrison/\">George Harrison</a>.</p><p>The evening session took place from 7-11.45pm. On track two of the four-track tape McCartney and Lennon recorded their vocals, and track three contained a harmonium part played by Lennon.</p><p>The song was completed on <a href=\"/1965/10/29/recording-mixing-we-can-work-it-out-day-tripper/\">29 October</a> with the addition of more vocals by McCartney and a second harmonium part from Lennon.</p><p><a href=\"/gallery/lyrics/lyrics-we-can-work-it-out_01/\" rel=\"attachment wp-att-108872\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSI4MDAiIGhlaWdodD0iNTE3IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgODAwIDUxNyI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" data-attachment-id=\"108872\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/lyrics/lyrics-we-can-work-it-out_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/lyrics-we-can-work-it-out_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1461,944\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Paul McCartney&amp;#8217;s handwritten lyrics for We Can Work It Out\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/lyrics-we-can-work-it-out_01-960x620.jpg\" data-src=\"/wp/media/lyrics-we-can-work-it-out_01-960x620.jpg\" alt=\"Paul McCartney's handwritten lyrics for We Can Work It Out\" width=\"800\" height=\"517\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-108872\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/lyrics-we-can-work-it-out_01-960x620.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/lyrics-we-can-work-it-out_01-580x375.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/lyrics-we-can-work-it-out_01-200x129.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/lyrics-we-can-work-it-out_01-768x496.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/lyrics-we-can-work-it-out_01.jpg 1461w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\"></a></p>\n<!--[googlesitekit-end-of-content]--><div style=\"font-size: 12px; margin: 10px 0 10px 0;\"><strong>Page last updated:</strong> 27 June 2023</div></div></div><div class=\"on-this-day-wrapper\"><h3>Also on this day...</h3><ul><li>2026: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2026/10/20/apple-corps-announces-beatles-story-museum-expansion-liverpool/\">Apple Corps announces Beatles Story museum expansion in Liverpool</a></li><li>2017: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2017/10/20/ringo-starr-all-starr-band-live-planet-hollywood-resort-las-vegas-4/\">Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Planet Hollywood Resort, Las Vegas</a></li><li>2017: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2017/10/20/paul-mccartney-live-itaipava-arena-fonte-nova-salvador/\">Paul McCartney live: Itaipava Arena Fonte Nova, Salvador</a></li><li>2016: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2016/10/20/ringo-starr-all-starr-band-live-segerstrom-center-arts-costa-mesa/\">Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Segerstrom Center for the Arts, Costa Mesa</a></li><li>2015: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2015/10/20/ringo-starr-all-starr-band-live-massey-hall-toronto/\">Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Massey Hall, Toronto</a></li><li>2001: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2001/10/20/paul-mccartney-live-madison-square-garden-new-york-city-5/\">Paul McCartney live: The Concert For New York City, Madison Square Garden, New York City</a></li><li>1998: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1998/10/20/album-release-vh1-storytellers-ringo-starr/\">Album release: VH1 Storytellers by Ringo Starr</a></li><li>1998: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1998/10/20/us-album-release-rushes-fireman-paul-mccartney-youth/\">US album release: Rushes by The Fireman (Paul McCartney and Youth)</a></li><li>1993: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1993/10/20/paul-mccartney-live-zenith-toulon/\">Paul McCartney live: Zénith, Toulon</a></li><li>1989: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1989/10/20/paul-mccartney-live-olympiahalle-munich/\">Paul McCartney live: Olympiahalle, Munich</a></li><li>1980: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1980/10/20/album-release-the-beatles-ballads/\">Album release: The Beatles Ballads</a></li><li>1978: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1978/10/20/mixing-reception-getting-closer-were-open-tonight-spin-it-on-again-old-siam-sir-to-you-arrow-through-me-after-ball-million-miles-winter-rose-love-awake-rockestra-theme-so-glad-to-see-you-here-wings/\">Mixing: Reception, Getting Closer, We’re Open Tonight, Spin It On, Again And Again And Again, Old Siam, Sir, To You, Arrow Through Me, After The Ball, Million Miles, Winter Rose, Love Awake, Rockestra Theme, So Glad To See You Here by Wings</a></li><li>1976: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1976/10/20/wings-live-empire-pool-london-2/\">Wings live: Empire Pool, London</a></li><li>1973: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1973/10/20/recording-angel-baby-john-lennon/\">Recording: Angel Baby by John Lennon</a></li><li>1972: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1972/10/20/editing-recording-live-and-let-die-wings/\">Editing, recording: Live And Let Die by Wings</a></li><li>1970: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1970/10/20/recording-when-the-wind-is-blowing-the-back-seat-of-my-car-paul-linda-mccartney/\">Recording: When The Wind Is Blowing, The Back Seat Of My Car by Paul and Linda McCartney</a></li><li>1969: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1969/10/20/mixing-live-peace-in-toronto-1969-plastic-ono-band-2/\">Mixing: Live Peace In Toronto 1969 by Plastic Ono Band</a></li><li>1969: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1969/10/20/us-single-release-cold-turkey-plastic-ono-band/\">US single release: Cold Turkey by Plastic Ono Band</a></li><li>1969: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1969/10/20/us-lp-release-wedding-album-john-lennon-yoko-ono/\">US album release: Wedding Album by John &amp; Yoko</a></li><li>1968: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1968/10/20/paul-mccartney-linda-eastman-holiday-new-york/\">Paul McCartney and Linda Eastman holiday in New York</a></li><li>1967: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1967/10/20/recording-the-fool-on-the-hill-hello-goodbye/\">Recording: The Fool On The Hill, Hello, Goodbye</a></li><li>1964: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1964/10/20/live-caird-hall-dundee-2/\">The Beatles live: Caird Hall, Dundee</a></li><li>1963: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1963/10/20/television-thank-your-lucky-stars-5/\">Television: Thank Your Lucky Stars</a></li><li>1962: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1962/10/20/live-majestic-ballroom-hull/\">The Beatles live: Majestic Ballroom, Hull</a></li><li>1961: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1961/10/20/live-knotty-ash-village-hall-liverpool-4/\">The Beatles live: Knotty Ash Village Hall, Liverpool</a></li><li>1961: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1961/10/20/live-cavern-club-liverpool-63/\">The Beatles live: Cavern Club, Liverpool (lunchtime)</a></li><li>1960: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1960/10/20/live-kaiserkeller-hamburg-17/\">The Beatles live: Kaiserkeller, Hamburg</a></li></ul><p>Want more? Visit the <a title=\"Day after day: the Beatles' history\" href=\"/history/\">Beatles history section</a>.</p></div><div class=\"gm-map\" style=\"position: relative;height: 390px; width: 100%;\"><iframe data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"about:blank\" name=\"gm-map-1\" allowfullscreen=\"\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/?geo_mashup_content=render-map&amp;map_data_key=030b4f80f2c1f44b3316e91d6c144f05&amp;height=390&amp;width=100%&amp;add_overview_control=false&amp;zoom=16&amp;enable_street_view=false&amp;map_type=G_HYBRID_MAP&amp;name=gm-map-1&amp;object_id=4616&amp;map_content=single\" style=\"position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: none; overflow: hidden;\" title=\"Geo Mashup Map\"></iframe></div>",
  "textContent": "Studio Two, EMI Studios, Abbey Road\nProducer: George Martin\nEngineer: Norman SmithThe Beatles had recorded ‘Day Tripper’ at Abbey Road on 16 October 1965. Four days later they began work on the other song on the double a-side single, ‘We Can Work It Out’. \n\n\n\n\n\nTwo recording sessions were scheduled on this day. The first lasted from 2.30-6.30pm, and saw the rehearsal of ‘We Can Work It Out’ plus the taping of two takes of the rhythm track. This included bass guitar by Paul McCartney, drums by Ringo Starr, John Lennon’s Gibson Jumbo acoustic guitar, and tambourine by George Harrison.The evening session took place from 7-11.45pm. On track two of the four-track tape McCartney and Lennon recorded their vocals, and track three contained a harmonium part played by Lennon.The song was completed on 29 October with the addition of more vocals by McCartney and a second harmonium part from Lennon.\nPage last updated: 27 June 2023Also on this day...2026: Apple Corps announces Beatles Story museum expansion in Liverpool2017: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Planet Hollywood Resort, Las Vegas2017: Paul McCartney live: Itaipava Arena Fonte Nova, Salvador2016: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Segerstrom Center for the Arts, Costa Mesa2015: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Massey Hall, Toronto2001: Paul McCartney live: The Concert For New York City, Madison Square Garden, New York City1998: Album release: VH1 Storytellers by Ringo Starr1998: US album release: Rushes by The Fireman (Paul McCartney and Youth)1993: Paul McCartney live: Zénith, Toulon1989: Paul McCartney live: Olympiahalle, Munich1980: Album release: The Beatles Ballads1978: Mixing: Reception, Getting Closer, We’re Open Tonight, Spin It On, Again And Again And Again, Old Siam, Sir, To You, Arrow Through Me, After The Ball, Million Miles, Winter Rose, Love Awake, Rockestra Theme, So Glad To See You Here by Wings1976: Wings live: Empire Pool, London1973: Recording: Angel Baby by John Lennon1972: Editing, recording: Live And Let Die by Wings1970: Recording: When The Wind Is Blowing, The Back Seat Of My Car by Paul and Linda McCartney1969: Mixing: Live Peace In Toronto 1969 by Plastic Ono Band1969: US single release: Cold Turkey by Plastic Ono Band1969: US album release: Wedding Album by John & Yoko1968: Paul McCartney and Linda Eastman holiday in New York1967: Recording: The Fool On The Hill, Hello, Goodbye1964: The Beatles live: Caird Hall, Dundee1963: Television: Thank Your Lucky Stars1962: The Beatles live: Majestic Ballroom, Hull1961: The Beatles live: Knotty Ash Village Hall, Liverpool1961: The Beatles live: Cavern Club, Liverpool (lunchtime)1960: The Beatles live: Kaiserkeller, HamburgWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
